        en: "THE ONE CONTRAST THAT ORGANISES THIS ENTIRE SECTION IS WITH THE OPERON THE CZECH BOOK ALREADY TAUGHT YOU. Lehninger defines the term first: “ We can define a transcriptional ground state as the inherent activity of promoters ” and transcriptional machinery in vivo in the absence of regulatory sequences (A p.1075). In bacteria, RNA polymerase generally has access to every promoter and can bind and initiate at some level of efficiency without any activator or repressor — the ground state is ON, which is exactly why lac and trp are taught as NEGATIVE control: the interesting regulatory event is a repressor switching something off. In eukaryotes, “ strong promoters are generally inactive in vivo in the absence of regulatory proteins ” — the ground state is OFF. Five differences follow from that inversion, and they are worth listing because the rest of the section is their elaboration. FIRST, access to eukaryotic promoters is restricted by the structure of chromatin, and activating transcription involves many changes to chromatin in the transcribed region. SECOND, although both positive and negative mechanisms exist, positive ones are more prominent — “ Almost every eukaryotic gene requires activation to be transcribed ”. THIRD, regulation involving lncRNAs is much more common. FOURTH, eukaryotic regulatory proteins are larger and more complex multimers. FIFTH, transcription in the nucleus is separated from translation in the cytoplasm in both space and time. Do not carry the operon model across: a Czech-layer answer that explains eukaryotic regulation with repressors and inducers has the sign of the whole system backwards.",
        cn: "**统摄整节的那个对照，正是与捷克教材已经教过的操纵子的对照。** Lehninger 先给术语下定义：**「我们可以把转录基态定义为，在没有调控序列的情况下，启动子」**与转录机器**在体内**的固有活性（A 第 1075 页）。在**细菌**中，RNA 聚合酶通常**能够到每一个启动子**，并且在**没有任何**激活蛋白或阻遏物的情况下就能结合并以某种效率起始——**基态是「开」**，而这恰恰就是 lac 和 trp 被当作**负调控**来讲的原因：那里有意思的调控事件是**阻遏物把什么东西关掉**。在**真核**中，**「强启动子在体内、若没有调控蛋白，通常是不活跃的」**——**基态是「关」**。由这个倒置产生**五个差别**，值得逐条列出，因为本节其余部分就是它们的展开。**第一**，真核启动子的可及性**受染色质结构限制**，而激活转录涉及被转录区域内**大量染色质结构的改变**。**第二**，虽然正负两种机制都存在，但**正调控更突出**——**「几乎每一个真核基因都需要被激活才能被转录」**。**第三**，涉及 **lncRNA** 的调控**常见得多**。**第四**，真核调控蛋白**更大、是更复杂的多聚体**。**第五**，核内的转录与胞质中的翻译在**空间和时间上都被分开**。**不要把操纵子模型照搬过来**：一份用阻遏物和诱导物来解释真核调控的答案，**把整个系统的正负号弄反了**。"
